  "findings": [
    "No surviving assemble16_native, endpoint_starts16_native, chase_step or chase_packet helper on any native profile. Native TP code-plane prepared packet routes and explicit widening/shift/OR reconstruction are inline; Series actual format-specific reconstruction remains.",
    "Tuple dead_mask16 is intentionally retained outlined and charged once per group dynamically. Compiler unrolling creates differing static sites. It uses actual prepared16-row dead-code projection, not sixteen erased point calls.",
    "Raw native/Series C1/C8 hot bodies have no prepared helper boundary in sampled cases; TP keeps geometry/state API bodies. ARM block-first alternative duplicates static state sites: one state call executes per request, and previous-geometry call executes except at block-first. Static count is not dynamic work.",
    "Native TP/Series paid group bodies emit SIMD reconstruction. Scattered endpoint shift uses NEON EXT, AVX2 VPERMD, AVX512 VALIGND. Ordered natural-plane endpoint shift can be scalarized/fused into the scalar memcpy consumer; not every paid-group body retains a vector shift. This is valid full-consumer lowering with automatic vectorizers disabled.",
    "Source pointer body+blocks[b].offset stays outside individual row copies. Ordinary projection remains the matched cheap point/scalar+libc alternative; paid groups include complete endpoint/used/dead decode and scattered scratch preparation.",
    "Native raw G/U group planes are natural u16/u32 lanes. TP per-code groups are16-byte planes and reconstruct G20/U12,G21/U13,G24/U16 explicitly. No custom per-point erased decode loop added."
  ],
